  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JM Governance and Anti-Corruption</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The task would support the completion of an anti-corruption and governance diagnostic, to inform the Jamaican government&apos;s anti-corruption and governance-strengthening program and build local government capacity to develop and monitor governance indicators.  WBI would provide technical assistance in parallel to the IDF grant. The development objective is to strengthen governance mechanisms and the fight against corruption through widening and deepening of accountability and transparency in public institutions. This objective will be achieved by: (i) broadening access to information by citizens under the Access to Information Act of 2002; and, (ii) development of in-country capacity on governance and anti-corruption (GAC) diagnostics through training of public and private sector agents in governance survey methodology and analysis, policy formulation, implementation strategies and governance activities monitoring.</narrative>
  </description>
